   "num": "01",
   "kind": "short",
   "intro": "<p>Honeybees collect nectar from flowers. The nectar of many flowers contains a high proportion of sucrose. In the hive, an enzyme added by the bees hydrolyses most of this sucrose into monosaccharides, and water evaporates from the nectar to form honey.</p>",
