   "num": "02",
   "kind": "short",
   "intro": "<p>In a DNA molecule, each adenine–thymine (A–T) base pair is held together by two hydrogen bonds and each cytosine–guanine (C–G) base pair by three hydrogen bonds.</p><p>Scientists extracted DNA from five species of bacteria, J to N. They heated each sample slowly in a salt solution and recorded the temperature at which the two strands of half of the DNA molecules had separated. Table 2 shows their results.</p><figure><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;max-width:100%\"><table class=\"tbl\"><caption>Table 2</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit\">Species</th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit\">Percentage of bases that are C or G</th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit\">Temperature at which half of the DNA has separated into single strands / °C</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit\">J</th><td>32</td><td>82.4</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit\">K</th><td>41</td><td>86.1</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit\">L</th><td>50</td><td>89.8</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit\">M</th><td>58</td><td>93.1</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:.85rem;color:inherit\">N</th><td>67</td><td>96.8</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figcaption class=\"small\">The values in Table 2 follow a published relationship between base composition and separation temperature in this salt solution; the species are not named.</figcaption></figure>",
