     "marks": 2,
     "stem": "Water molecules are small but polar. A little water crosses the cell-surface membranes of the carrot cells directly through the phospholipid bilayer, but most passes through channel proteins.<br>Explain why the phospholipid bilayer limits the movement of water, <strong>and</strong> explain how channel proteins allow water to cross the membrane more quickly.",
