     "model": "At 0.30 mol dm⁻³ the root F cylinders lost 2.4 % of their mass but the root S cylinders gained 2.4 %, and at 0.40 mol dm⁻³ root F lost 5.9 % but root S lost only 1.1 %. At 0.30 mol dm⁻³ water moved out of the F cells by osmosis, so their water potential was higher than that of the solution, but water moved into the S cells, so their water potential was lower than that of the solution. The cells of root S therefore have a lower, more negative water potential than those of root F.",
